@playwright
Feature: CartTrace

  Demonstrates recording one Playwright trace per Gherkin step. Running `mvn test` in this
  module drives a real browser through the steps below, writes a self-contained trace zip for
  each one under target/playwright-traces/, and stamps each zip's path onto its step in
  target/specbinder-reports/specs/CartTrace.specb.json.

  Scenario: A fresh cart starts empty
    Given I open the cart page
    Then the cart total should be "0.00"

  Scenario: Adding an item updates the total
    Given I open the cart page
    When I add "Apple" to the cart
    Then the cart total should be "1.50"

  Scenario: Adding two items sums their prices
    Given I open the cart page
    When I add "Apple" to the cart
    And I add "Cherries" to the cart
    Then the cart total should be "5.70"

  Scenario: Clearing the cart resets the total
    Given I open the cart page
    When I add "Banana" to the cart
    And I clear the cart
    Then the cart total should be "0.00"

  Scenario: Intentional failure, so one trace captures a red step
    Given I open the cart page
    When I add "Banana" to the cart
    Then the cart total should be "99.99"

  Scenario Outline: Each catalogue item lands at its own price
    Given I open the cart page
    When I add "<item>" to the cart
    Then the cart total should be "<price>"

    Examples:
      | item     | price |
      | Apple    | 1.50  |
      | Banana   | 0.75  |
      | Cherries | 4.20  |
